From d4c3c30a156b45aa41c6ec79ebb160c3d2e21df4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:36:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Big screen: faster slide changes (measured, no behaviour
 change)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the projector stage (photo deck, 4x CPU throttle, 20 Mbit):
script ~0 ms; ~145 ms decoding + ~230 ms rasterising the photo inside
the frame that shows the new slide. Median worst frame per change
222-298 ms -> 85-105 ms; first change and fast-click cases no worse.

Stage (hanns_present.js)
- screen-sized renditions: a worker makes a copy of oversized JPEGs at
  this screen's size (header-sized decode, aspect kept by construction),
  used from the next paint on; JPEG only — PNG/GIF/SVG/WebP untouched
- the worker yields to the room: stopped on every slide change, job
  re-queued, resumes once the slide has settled; one job at a time,
  forward-first; only converts photos already downloaded (no extra
  network); a crashed worker can't stall the queue
- decode-ahead window (next, next+1, previous) of what will be painted;
  neighbours' bytes fetched straight away
- magnifier / zoom regions put the full-resolution originals back
- no Worker/OffscreenCanvas/createImageBitmap -> exactly as before

Core (hanns_core.js): mediaSrc() consults renditions registered by the
stage (none anywhere else); mediaSrcRaw/setMediaRendition exported;
paintImageBox remembers the original (data-full-src)

Server (consumers.py): goto stores the slide and reads just that one row
in one thread hop (it loaded every slide of the deck to send one):
9.3 -> 3.6 ms median; equivalence test incl. reordered/past-the-end/empty
